  HONEST READING.  The register's stated rule (alpha ~ 1/2 => against P1) is
  logically reversed: x^{1/2+o(1)} = o(x), so square-root cancellation supports
  P1 rather than refuting it.  The only genuine finite-range refutation of P1
  would be an arc with |C_I(x)|/x bounded below on the tested range, and no arc
  here shows that.  Conversely, finite prefix data cannot establish o(x) either
  (a finitely supported perturbation of lambda has identical data and different
  asymptotics).  No asymptotic statement is claimed.
